{
  "abstract": "A measure-theoretic account of projected stochastic histories distinguishes observed Markov order, history-state compression, classical factorization, and quantum CP-divisibility. The exact classical construction does not derive noncommutative observables; the separate canonical operational q79 source is retained. Forty-eight frozen BEQ results are explained through coherent history witnesses, finite HEOM profiles, bounded optical readout, physical tangent and nuisance domains, charged molecular lines, conditional geometric repair, metric-aware error transport, and held-out clock and response tests. Exact compatibility and finite numerical profiles do not select a physical q79-FMO correspondence. Same-source preparation, calibrated intervention and observation, controlled physical transport, and an independently fixed clock remain required.",
